PEGPU AI Web UI and Model Router
================================

This directory contains PEGPU-specific app code for the embedded AI web UI,
model discovery, runtime management, and OpenAI/llama.cpp-compatible request
routing.

It is not an unmodified copy of llama.cpp, llama-swap, or their release
artifacts.

llama.cpp provenance
--------------------

The embedded chat UI and API surface are based on llama.cpp server conventions,
the llama.cpp web UI surface, and llama.cpp-compatible HTTP APIs. PEGPU modifies
that app-facing surface for:

- local macOS and VM runtime selection
- external GPU offload controls
- model discovery across Hugging Face and LM Studio cache locations
- multiple model entries routed through configured runtime instances
- packaged app integration instead of a standalone llama.cpp server bundle

PEGPU does not store llama.cpp runtime binaries in this source repository.
Release packages bundle the latest llama.cpp ARM64 runtime build available at
PEGPU release time from openresearchtools/llama-cpp-arm64-builds. Runtime
binaries such as llama-server, rpc-server, and libllama/libggml libraries carry
their own license files. Additional llama.cpp and TurboQuant runtime versions
remain user-managed through the /core runtime release workflow.

llama.cpp is MIT licensed. The generated PEGPU legal bundle includes the
llama.cpp MIT license as:

  licenses/llama.cpp-MIT.txt

llama-swap provenance
---------------------

The model-routing behavior is based on llama-swap's request-routing model.
PEGPU modifies that model to route llama.cpp-compatible API requests across
configured macOS and VM runtimes, including:

- VM/CUDA and macOS/Metal runtime pairs
- multiple model aliases served by the same runtime instance
- sessions detached from a single fixed llama-server process
- app-managed downloads, runtime launches, and bridge endpoints

llama-swap is MIT licensed. The generated PEGPU legal bundle includes the
llama-swap MIT license as:

  licenses/llama-swap-MIT.txt

